<title>TURKEY: Turk Petkim 9-mth profits rise 4.3 pct.</title>
<headline>Turk Petkim 9-mth profits rise 4.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-Sept 1996 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)	5,722.18  vs  5,485.88</p>
<p>    Net profit			17,166.54  vs 16,457.65</p>
<p>    Net sales			 50,208.78  vs 40,890.39</p>
<p>    Operating profit		11,800.94  vs 18,857.33</p>
<p>    Exceptional income	    22,345.82  vs  8,613.69</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense		128.17  vs     62.94</p>
<p>    Interest paid			342.95  vs    574.54</p>
<p>    Exceptional expense	    1,249.93  vs    993.34</p>
<p>    Total debts		     23,672.05  vs 14,388.40</p>
<p>    Equity			    83,402.51  vs 55,856.10</p>
<p>    Capital			    3,000.00  vs  3,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkey's largely state owned petrochemicals company Petkim - Petrokimya Holding A.S. is slated for privatisation, with 96 percent of its shares held by the privatisation agency OIB.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 79.3 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in September.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875 EKS</p>
</text>
